// A #when condition is an expression, so it may start with `!', `(' or `-'.
// It was refused as "! is a reserved word and cannot be a name": the check
// meant for `#variable out' ran after #when too.
#variable B = 0
#variable C = 0
#variable D = 0
#when !B
  C = 1
#end
#when (B == 0) && !(B > 0)
  D = 2
#end
